One step of the depth-n union fold reads a depth, an index, and an accumulator from its packed input, and takes the bit-source to be the index plus two to that depth. If the D-side atom at the next depth for that bit-source is empty, the accumulator is unchanged. Otherwise the found flag becomes one, and the stored code is the union of the accumulated code with the new atom code when a genuine atom was already found, and is the new atom code when none was.
